Well, you are returning "list", even when coroutine has not finished yet. Are you using viewModel? A great solution would be:
On your viewModel, create a liveData to store your list
class myViewModel: ViewModel() {
     val myList = mutableLiveDataOf<List<Post>>
}

On your viewModel create a function that only calls the coroutine:
fun getList() : List<Post> {
    CoroutineScope(IO).launch {
        var info = db.userDao().getAll()
        lmyList.postValue(info) // Here you are updating you list 
    }

    return list
}

Observe your list from activity/fragment:
   class myFrag: Fragment() {
     /*some code*/
     myViewModel.myList.observe(viewLifecycleOwner, Observer{ list ->
          if(!list.isNullOrEmpty()){
               /* Here you'll have your list and can set it on the adapter*/
          }
     })

   }

